# Define the Track Sizes

These properties take a space‑separated list of track sizes. Each value creates a new column or row.

```css
.container {
  grid-template-columns: 100px 200px 1fr;
  grid-template-rows: 80px auto 80px;
}
```
- First column: 100px, second: 200px, third: 1 fraction of remaining space.
- First row: 80px, second: `auto` (height based on content), third: 80px.

You can use any CSS length, percentage, `auto`, or the powerful `fr` unit.

slides.codeSnippet:
.gallery {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(250px, 1fr));
  gap: 16px;
}
